{%- macro signal_text(s, kinds=None) -%}
{%- if s.kind.value == 'zero_traffic_errors' -%}
Receive errors advanced {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.delta_input_errors) }} (~{{ s.values.errors_per_second }}/s) while the device-reported input rate was {{ s.values.input_rate_pps if s.values.input_rate_pps != -1 else '?' }} pps{% if s.values.last_input_minutes != -1 %} and last input was {{ window(s.values.last_input_minutes) }} prior{% endif %}. Errors are accumulating without valid traffic: the fault is at the link, not in the traffic.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'unattributed_rx_dominant' -%}
{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.unattributed_rx) }} of {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.input_errors) }} input errors ({{ '%.1f'|format(100 * s.values.unattributed_rx / s.values.input_errors) }}%) fall in no named bucket, consistent with symbol-level corruption{% if s.values.runts != -1 %}. runts/UnderSize: {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.runts) }}{% endif %}.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'runts_dominant_no_collisions' -%}
Runts dominate the input-error total with zero collision activity: frames are not surviving to the MAC.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'fcs_fraction_active' -%}
FCS errors are {{ '%.1f'|format(100 * s.values.fcs_fraction) }}% of input errors: frames arriving but corrupted (marginal signal).
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'buffer_group_dominant' -%}
{% if s.values.buffer_group is defined %}Overrun/ignored/no-buffer/input-queue drops account for {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.buffer_group) }} of {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.input_errors) }} input errors in the window: congestion, not media.{% else %}{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.discards) }} {{ s.values.direction }} discards at meaningful rate: frames arrived intact and were dropped (oversubscription, policer, or ring sizing), not media.{% endif %}
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'discards_without_congestion_signature' -%}
{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.discards) }} {{ s.values.direction }} discards at meaningful rate with no buffer-pressure signature (overrun/ignored/no-buffer flat): consistent with policy drops (unallowed VLAN, ACL, storm-control), not congestion.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'reliability_degraded' -%}
Interface reliability {{ s.values.reliability }}/255: the device's own error-weighted average reports the link as degraded (255/255 is healthy).
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'half_duplex_link' -%}
The link is running {{ s.values.duplex }} duplex at {{ s.values.speed }}. Modern switched networks negotiate full duplex everywhere; half duplex here points at a negotiation problem or a legacy/failing endpoint, and makes the collision counters meaningful evidence.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'collision_activity_on_erroring_link' -%}
{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.late_collisions) }} late collisions and {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.collisions) }} collisions accompany the receive errors: collision activity points at negotiation, so the errors cannot be pinned on the medium alone{% if s.values.neighbor_duplex in ('?', '') %} — and no neighbor reports its duplex, so a mismatch can be neither confirmed nor cleared from here{% endif %}.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'late_collisions_full_duplex' -%}
{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.late_collisions) }} late collisions on a {{ s.values.duplex }}-duplex link{% if s.values.neighbor_duplex is defined and s.values.neighbor_duplex not in ('?', '') %} (neighbor {{ s.values.neighbor_name }}{% if s.values.neighbor_platform is defined and s.values.neighbor_platform not in ('?', '') %}, {{ s.values.neighbor_platform }},{% endif %} reports {{ s.values.neighbor_duplex }}){% endif %}: negotiation/duplex mismatch, fixed via CLI.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'giants_with_mtu_mismatch' -%}
Giants dominate ({{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.giants) }}, local MTU {{ s.values.mtu }}): consistent with an MTU mismatch between ends; far-end MTU unknown.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'speed_below_capability' -%}
Link negotiated {{ s.values.speed }} on a {{ s.values.media_type }} port{% if kinds and ('unattributed_rx_dominant' in kinds or 'runts_dominant_no_collisions' in kinds or 'zero_traffic_errors' in kinds) %} while symbol-level corruption dominates the receive errors: 1000BaseT needs all four pairs, and a damaged pair forces exactly this fallback — one damaged-pair story explains the speed, the corruption{% if 'interface_resets' in kinds %}, and the resets{% endif %}. Still consistent with a genuinely 100M endpoint — the TDR resolves it{% else %}. Consistent with damaged pairs, but also consistent with a 100M endpoint — unresolved{% endif %}.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'bytes_per_frame_above_mtu' -%}
Byte counter implies ~{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.bytes_per_frame) }} B/frame against MTU {{ s.values.mtu }}: errored octets are being counted.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'dom_rx_out_of_range' -%}
DOM receive power {{ '%.1f'|format(s.values.dom_rx_power_dbm) }} dBm outside {{ '%g'|format(s.values.dom_rx_low_dbm) }}..{{ '%g'|format(s.values.dom_rx_high_dbm) }} dBm: degraded optical path.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'fault_onset_estimate' -%}
The lifetime total at the current rate spans {{ window(s.values.onset_minutes) }} — matching the {{ window(s.values.last_input_minutes) }} since the last valid frame. The fault has likely run at this rate since valid traffic stopped: a concrete date to correlate with change windows.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'zero_delta_nonzero_lifetime' -%}
The lifetime counter is large ({{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.values() | first) }}) but did not move between this tool's two observations: old event, not an incident.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'low_fcs_does_not_clear_media' -%}
FCS-Err is only {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.fcs_errors) }} of {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.input_errors) }}. Low FCS does not rule out media faults: symbol corruption and short frames are discarded before the FCS check. Verdict retained.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'interface_resets' -%}
{{ s.values.interface_resets }} interface resets{% if s.values.resets_per_year is defined %} (~{{ s.values.resets_per_year }}/year over the counter's life){% endif %}.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'errors_stopped_after_clear' -%}
If errors stop advancing after a coordinated manual counter clear and repoll, reclassify HISTORIC_NOT_ACTIVE.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'errors_resumed' -%}
If the counter advances again on a future run, the case reopens and is reclassified.
{%- else -%}
{{ s.kind.value }}: {{ s.values }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro next_steps(r) -%}
{%- set media = ((r.stats.media_type if r.stats else '') or '') | lower | replace('-', '') -%}
{%- set copper = 'baset' in media -%}
{%- set fiber = r.stats and r.stats.dom_rx_power_dbm is not none -%}
{%- set category = r.verdict.category.value -%}
{%- set bundle_case = r.verdict.member_findings and not r.parent_portchannel -%}
{%- set clear_target = 'the culpable member interface (the bundle aggregates its members)' if bundle_case else 'this interface' -%}
{%- if category == 'PHYSICAL_MEDIA' -%}
{%- if copper -%}
  Next steps — non-disruptive: identify the attached device and its native
    speed; inspect the patch cord and the jack{% if r.stats and r.stats.interface_resets %}; correlate the error history
    with the interface resets{% endif %}. DOM is not implemented on this copper port —
    expected, not a finding.
  Disruptive, coordinate first: TDR (test cable-diagnostics tdr) on {{ r.case.interface }};
    a manual counter clear on {{ clear_target }} and a repoll at 24 h to
    establish a clean baseline.
{%- elif fiber -%}
  Next steps — non-disruptive: inspect and clean the fiber connectors and
    patch panel; check the transceiver's DOM receive-power trend (this
    reading: {{ '%.1f'|format(r.stats.dom_rx_power_dbm) }} dBm — a single reading,
    not a trend); verify the optic is seated.
  Disruptive, coordinate first: a manual counter clear and a repoll at 24 h;
    replace the transceiver if DOM stays out of range.
{%- else -%}
  Next steps — non-disruptive: inspect the physical path.{% if media and not copper %} DOM could not
    be read from the transceiver output on this port — check it manually.{% endif %}
  Disruptive, coordinate first: a manual counter clear on {{ clear_target }} and
    a repoll at 24 h.
{%- endif -%}
{%- elif category == 'LINK_NEGOTIATION' -%}
{%- set phone = r.stats and ('phone' in (r.stats.neighbor_platform or '') | lower or (r.stats.neighbor_name or '').startswith('SEP')) -%}
  Next steps: fix via CLI — align speed/duplex (and MTU where giants
    dominate) on both ends.{% if phone %} The endpoint is a managed IP phone: its
    speed/duplex is set from the call manager (CUCM), not at the jack.{% endif %} Not a
    media dispatch.
{%- elif category == 'CONGESTION_BUFFER' -%}
{%- set policy = r.verdict.signals | selectattr('kind.value', 'equalto', 'discards_without_congestion_signature') | list -%}
{% if policy %}  Next steps: check the port's policy first — trunk allowed VLANs, ACL hit
    counters, storm-control — before provisioning capacity; the buffer-side
    counters are flat. Not a media dispatch.
{%- else %}  Next steps: review oversubscription, policers, and buffer/ring sizing on
    this path. Not a media dispatch.
{%- endif %}
{%- elif category == 'HISTORIC_NOT_ACTIVE' -%}
  Next steps: coordinate a manual counter clear, then requeue for a future
    run. Do not dispatch anyone.
{%- endif -%}
{%- if r.stats and r.stats.vpc_status and r.stats.vpc_status | lower == 'up' and category in ('PHYSICAL_MEDIA', 'LINK_NEGOTIATION', 'CONGESTION_BUFFER') %}
  This port serves vPC {{ r.stats.vpc_number }} and the vPC is up: the peer switch
    carries a leg to the same host, so member-level remediation can be
    hitless — verify the peer leg is healthy first, and check it for the
    same errors.
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro dq_text(f) -%}
{%- if f.kind.value == 'stale_poll_timestamp' -%}
CSV poll timestamp is {{ window(f.values.staleness_minutes) }} old at report time; its rates describe that period.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'interval_from_ingest_time' -%}
Interval ({{ window(f.values.interval_minutes) }}) derived from host-side timestamps, not device time.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'delta_source_disagreement' -%}
Delta sources disagree: iftriage run-to-run {{ '{:,}'.format(f.values.delta_tool) }} vs CSV change {{ '{:,}'.format(f.values.delta_csv) }}; the tool's own delta is used for rate math; the CSV's delta window is not stated in the export and has proven inconsistent across rows — confirm it in the Splunk search.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'reconciliation_skew' -%}
Input-error reconciliation is off by {{ f.values.residual }} — consistent with the counters advancing (~{{ f.values.errors_per_second }}/s) between the two show commands, not an accounting problem.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'counter_reconciliation_failed' -%}
Input-error reconciliation does not balance: residual {{ '{:,}'.format(f.values.residual) }} ({{ '%.1f'|format(100 * f.values.residual_fraction) }}%).
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'no_second_observation' -%}
Single observation: no earlier sample could be subtracted.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'ratio_out_of_range' -%}
A ratio fell outside 0..100% and was suppressed ({{ f.values.detail }}).
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'null_rule_input' -%}
Unknown input(s) to a fired rule: {{ f.values.fields }}. Confidence capped.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'poll_timezone_assumed_utc' -%}
The CSV _time column carries no timezone; UTC was assumed.
{%- else -%}
{{ f.kind.value }}: {{ f.values }}
{%- endif -%}
